    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "This NVIDIA chip is smaller than a bank card. How small is one switch?",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.24,
        "window": 3.8,
        "fill": 0.853
      },
      {
        "scene": "crowd",
        "text": "And it isn't one big brain. It's 16,384 small ones, all working at once.",
        "start": 4.1,
        "seconds": 4.7,
        "window": 5.3,
        "fill": 0.887
      },
      {
        "scene": "desk",
        "text": "They split up every single frame of your game, so each one only colours its own patch of dots, over and over.",
        "start": 9.4,
        "seconds": 4.98,
        "window": 5.43,
        "fill": 0.917
      },
      {
        "scene": "city",
        "text": "So where are they all? Lift the silicon out and zoom in: it looks like a city at night, seen from a plane.",
        "start": 14.83,
        "seconds": 4.73,
        "window": 5.2,
        "fill": 0.91
      },
      {
        "scene": "dive",
        "text": "But dive into just one core. What's doing the maths? No magic. Just tiny switches.",
        "start": 20.03,
        "seconds": 4.43,
        "window": 4.83,
        "fill": 0.917
      },
      {
        "scene": "bits",
        "text": "Each one is either on or off, a one or a zero. That's really it. And every single colour you see is built from them.",
        "start": 24.87,
        "seconds": 5.4,
        "window": 5.8,
        "fill": 0.931
      },
      {
        "scene": "before",
        "text": "The chip before this one already held 28B of them. Back then, that sounded like a lot.",
        "start": 30.67,
        "seconds": 4.5,
        "window": 4.93,
        "fill": 0.913
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "This one packs 76B, all on a piece of silicon smaller than a bank card.",
        "start": 35.6,
        "seconds": 3.65,
        "window": 4.2,
        "fill": 0.869
      },
      {
        "scene": "back",
        "text": "So zoom all the way back out, past the switches, past the cores, past the fans, to this NVIDIA chip.",
        "start": 39.8,
        "seconds": 4.95,
        "window": 5.4,
        "fill": 0.917
      }
    ]
  },
